{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Before the hoary head you shall rise.</b> One might say even an old transgressor — therefore Scripture says זָקֵן — זָקֵן means only one who has acquired wisdom (Kiddushin 32)." "<b>And you shall honor the face of an old man.</b> What is honoring? He must not sit in his place and must not contradict his words. One might say he could shut his eyes as though he did not see him? Therefore it says <b>and you shall fear your Elohim</b> — for this matter is delivered to the heart of the one who does it, since no one recognizes it but him, and any matter delivered to the heart has 'and you shall fear your Elohim' said of it (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:19.793334097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}